<title>HONG KONG: HK's Solartech debuts at HK$1.50 each.</title>
<headline>HK's Solartech debuts at HK$1.50 each.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hong Kong-based cable maker and exporter Solartech International Holdings Ltd made their trading debut at HK$1.50 per share in Hong Kong, compared with an issue price of HK$1.20.  </p>
<p>Solartech offered 125 million new shares at HK$1.20 each, with an attachment of warrants in the proportion of one warrant 1071.HK for every five shares.</p>
<p>Its flotation was 122.1 times subscribed.</p>
<p>Solartech said proceeds would be used to expand manufacturing capacity, to improve its customer network in China and to set up a joint venture.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
